WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
Esports competition is grueling and can wear down even the best pro players. But

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.330
fans don’t only want to watch players compete, they want to care about them too.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.600
"And I made it my goal. I wanted people to recognize me.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.660
I wanted people to know, like hey, that’s Nadeshot. That’s Nadeshot."

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.640
And nowhere was the balance between high-level competitor

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.300
and internet personality better realized than in a young kid from Chicago.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.880
"YouTube how the f*** ya doin."

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:31.040
His name is Matthew “Nadeshot” Haag and he is one of esports’ biggest stars.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.800
This is his story.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.400
One of the most influential players in the history of competitive Call of Duty

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.020
actually started off hating the game.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.800
"The first experience I had with Call of Duty was CoD 2, and that was when I first got my Xbox 360

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.180
I put the game in and I literally got spawn trapped for the next five minutes

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:58.980
and I never played it after that. I absolutely hated it because of that one experience."

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.580
But though he didn’t fall in love with CoD 2, he loved gaming so much that his mom

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.980
made him get a job at McDonald’s just to get him away from the screen.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:12.140
"I think when any parent sees their child doing something that's really out of the ordinary

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.100
that's gonna raise a lot of red flags so I can imagine what they thought about it

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.140
and I think that's the main reason why my mom made me get a job because she was

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.120
worried that I was just gonna waste my life away behind my computer screen."

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.900
"Like eight hours a day, eight to ten
hours a day we would just grind

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.100
Search and Destroy public playlists because that was what was fun for us."

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.240
Seeking greater competition,
Nadeshot and his friends went to

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.960
GameBattles, a platform that would land him his first big break.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:44.260
There, he met MerK, and the two were approached by OpTic Nerve during Modern Warfare 2.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.000
Nerve offered the two gamers a chance to build an OpTic roster.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.540
Since 2009, OpTic Gaming were committed to creating video content.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.600
While they were going back to the organization’s roots by fielding a competitive roster,

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.240
the entertainment side of the industry was their focus.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.560
Even at this early point in the team’s history, there were hints that the

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.880
route to popularity didn’t have to rely on tournament results.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.300
Fans could be earned online and introduced to competition,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.480
while esports fans could find more to like about these competitors on YouTube.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.560
And H3CZ would eventually bring Nadeshot around to the OpTic way of thinking:

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:22.100
content, daily whenever possible, was the path to a dedicated following.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.380
"I met him when he was a lot younger but very pleasant.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:31.320
Just smiles all around. Fun guy to be around and to talk to

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.000
and that was the first time I actually had ever met a pro player before.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.640
So I was kind of just taken back, like what is this relationship dynamic?"

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.840
Though they managed to defeat heavyweights Team EnVyUs at Dallas,

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.080
OpTic finished eigth.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.200
And while they still received strong fan support, not long after the event,

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:53.700
H3CZ called Nadeshot and told him that the rest of the team wanted him gone.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:03:00.320
At the time, Hector convinced Nade to continue with content creation and to stay on with OpTic in that role.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.620
In Nadeshot he saw a rare combination: even though he wasn’t naturally

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.700
comfortable in front of a camera, he was a strong competitor.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.240
But also someone approachable that fans could identify with.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.340
Nade told his fans that he was no longer with the team,

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.800
and although he said it was a voluntary move, he later admitted that it had been a crushing experience.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.980
In terms of competition, it wasn’t clear when or even if Nade would return.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:31.520
But he threw himself into the business of content creation despite still having school and a part-time job.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.480
"Any time that I was at home, I was playing Call of Duty or working on content production

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.340
for my YouTube channel or my livestream."

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.880
That drive showed H3CZ that his investment in Nade might still pay off.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:48.880
And when the competitive team needed a replacement for Rambo at MLG Dallas 2011,

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.400
Nadeshot got the call.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.240
"Obviously I haven't played in a while so I'm curious to see what happens."

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:58.440
After helping the team place third, Nadeshot went back to creating content.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.580
But H3CZ could see the competitive fire still burning in Nadeshot’s eyes,

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:06.720
and created a second OpTic team, called OpTic Nation, for him to run.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.880
Though that team had limited competitive success,

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.720
H3CZ saw that Nadeshot’s content was doing something different:

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:17.520
Nadeshot understood it too, as he consistently produced content

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:23.440
that bridged the gap between the esports and gaming audiences, by offering a glimpse into his personal life

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:29.120
"Well this gameplay is gonna wrap up I kicked the s*** out of my brother and he's older than me.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.400
He was pretty pissed cause I got Kyle Korver and the Chicago Bulls and Derrick Rose."

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.100
"YouTube, how the f*** you doin'. Hey guys it's Nadeshot, and I'm doing a vlog from my

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.540
iPad that I actually got for my birthday. My grandparents got it for me.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.200
I hope you guys can't hear these dogs in the background because they are loud as hell."

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.140
"Alright go ahead."

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:47.500
"YouTube!

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.440
How the f*** are you doing?

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:51.700
Merry Christmas!

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.000
From Nadeshot, grandfather."

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:57.380
With his subscriber base on YouTube continuing to grow,

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:00.860
Nadeshot announced that he had finally quit his job at McDonald’s.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.300
He was all-in on Call of Duty.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:10.320
In June 2011, OpTic Nation placed 6th at MLG Columbus while the main OpTic Gaming squad took first.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:14.980
But Nade saw a shot at glory with another team, and briefly joined nV

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.900
for MLG Anaheim and MLG Raleigh.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:23.140
After a couple of events with NV, Nadeshot finally had another chance on OpTic’s main roster

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:26.980
at the biggest Call of Duty event yet: CoD XP 2011.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:32.140
Featuring a million-dollar prize pool and a post-tournament performance by Kanye West,

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:36.380
it was Activision’s first big step into figuring out CoD esports.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:41.580
The tournament may not have had the most competitive field and it featured Modern Warfare 3,

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.360
a game that wasn’t even out yet. But with Nadeshot OpTic won,

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:50.800
again raising questions about why he was sidelined when both his skill and popularity

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:53.240
could be better harnessed by the organization.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.580
But he stepped back down, restarted OpTic Nation, and waited.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.440
He waited for over a year, during which he played with a number of mix teams,

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.800
none of which had wins at any major event.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.080
However uneventful 2012 was in Nadeshot’s career,

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:13.300
it was the year in which he would suffer his most significant loss.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.980
"Hey guys what's going on, it's Nadeshot from OpTic Gaming.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.120
And some of you may have heard.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:23.340
In the past couple days on Twitter if you follow me or anybody else.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.940
That my mom actually passed away at the age of 47

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.780
on  Saturday night, she died in her sleep.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:37.580
It's kind of a gruesome detail but, just want to let you guys know that I am truly am thankful

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.980
for all the support that you've shown me on Twitter and all my social media outlets like Facebook."

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:46.740
Nadeshot’s Mother, Christina, had sometimes criticized his gaming,

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.600
but in time came to support his esports dream.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:55.440
"I think she would approve now, for sure. I think things have kind of taken off to a point where

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.320
she wouldn't have a choice at this point. I mean, just the things I've been able to do for my family

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.000
and the things I've been able to do for myself in my career.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.640
I think she would completely understand it."

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:07.340
While Nadeshot's 2012 had been tumultuous,

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:11.540
OpTic had been experiencing one of its most successful periods in Call of Duty.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:15.280
Dominating Modern Warfare 3 with up and coming star Scump.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:19.400
But Nadeshot wasn’t satisfied with watching the team’s success from the sidelines

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:24.300
so he convinced H3CZ and the team to add him as a starter in place of Rambo.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:28.840
"I convinced them to let me back on the team. So like it was my time to shine.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:33.980
I had all this pressure on my shoulders because nobody really agreed with the roster move,

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:38.680
they did not want to see Rambo off the team, but for me, this was me trying to come into my own…”

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:43.280
With Nadeshot in the lineup, OpTiC headed to UMG Chicago for the first ever LAN

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.840
event on the recently released Call of Duty: Black Ops 2.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:50.400
"We were either going to be so incredibly successful and shock the world,

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.320
or I was going to be the laughing stock of the competitive community."

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:58.700
In spite of the pressure, Nadeshot rose to the occasion and the team found themselves in

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:01.640
the grand finals against an ACHES-led compLexity.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:05.820
"That was the biggest rivalry for us, dude. ACHES always kicked OpTic’s ass.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.720
For whatever reason, he always beat us."

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.280
"He was just talking so much s*** before this match even started.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.320
We're sitting on main stage and this dude is just doing what he does best.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.660
And he's trying to get into everybody's head.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:20.860
And I was just so focused on winning the match that I really wasn't getting in on it."

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:24.160
But Nadeshot and OpTic would have the last laugh this time

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:26.900
and the fallout from their triumph got a little heated.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:58.380
(Casting)

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:04.860
Nadeshot and ACHES already had a history, but this incident would escalate their rivalry to the next level.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:13.340
"This is a cringey and embarrassing video, but it set-off the entirety of the success that CoD had,

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:17.800
I’m cringing watching myself, but this is a moment that I will never forget."

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:24.900
As 2013 began, Nadeshot finally signed with Red Bull after over a year of speculation regarding a deal.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:31.200
"Probably the most humbling experience of my life. For me, this is something that was a dream come true.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:36.780
It marked not just a landmark moment in Nade’s career, but for Call of Duty esports as a whole.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:41.700
Although OpTic managed to beat ACHES and compLexity again at the Call of Duty Championship,

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:47.440
a disappointing third place finish marked the beginning of a majorless slump for the team in 2013.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:51.160
But OpTic was changing. They added a gaming house in Chicago,

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:55.960
and continued to grow in popularity despite their lack of first-place finishes.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:59.020
Even when the results weren’t there, the content was.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:02.360
"If you enjoyed it make sure you click the like button. Favourite if you really enjoyed it. Comment, let me know

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.480
what you thought of the video. Any constructive criticism always helps"

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:05.920
"Bro can you stop asking for likes bro?"

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:07.300
"Yeah just exit the video"

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:08.740
"Can you stop asking for like bro?"

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:12.560
Nadeshot, now living in a team house and fully immersed in Call of Duty,

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:16.460
took a moment to reflect on how big this opportunity really was.

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:19.420
"And this is something that I've always wanted

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:26.320
And my mom never really saw it going anywhere.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:31.300
And she really worried about me. She really worried for me if this was gonna work out.

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:35.180
If I was kind of screwing my own life up by quitting school.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:39.020
But I always saw school as something like it's always going to be there

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.940
and it's always going to be my backup plan.

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:50.380
The fact that all this has worked out so far and the growth has continued, I really do appreciate it guys."

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:56.340
A few months later, JKap replaced MerK and the team finished 2nd at the MLG Fall Invitational,

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:02.000
OpTic’s best placement since UMG Chicago with ACHES playing foil to Nadeshot’s hopes

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.680
in a backbreaking comeback.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:30.420
(Casting)

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:34.020
2013 had shown OpTic that the demands of both competition

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:38.180
and content creation could take their toll on players that were unprepared,

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:42.520
but Nadeshot had always been able to satisfy both sides of that equation.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:47.220
Still, H3CZ acknowledged that the situation must have been frustrating.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.200
2014 would be the year of Call of Duty: Ghosts,

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:55.680
a polarizing game within the esport’s scene that ultimately led to a roster shake-up on OpTic.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:59.900
The team would keep Nade and Scump, but add Clayster and ProoFy.

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:05.640
However, despite the line-up changes, it would end up being a year OpTic fans would prefer to forget.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:12.220
Although the two had arguments in the past, an incident early in the year saw Nadeshot and Scump butt heads,

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:15.280
with Scump actually issuing an ultimatum to the team:

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:19.160
get rid of Nade, or he would leave and go to Team EnVyUs.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:26.100
He basically thought that I was the reason why we couldn't win, he just wasn't a fan of me,

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:26.920
he didn't like me anymore

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:30.820
Nadeshot actually went to H3CZ and offered to step down,

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:34.120
saying that Scump was the better player and deserved the spot.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:38.640
But given the way Scump had approached the situation, H3CZ decided to keep Nadeshot.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.980
It would work out, as Scump quickly asked to come back.

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:43.780
After a disappointing start to the year,

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:48.620
the team again managed a third-place finish at the Call of Duty Championship.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:52.940
Once again, they lost a close, important series to  compLexity.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.240
(Casting)

00:12:56.280 --> 00:13:00.660
Morale wasn’t great as the year continued, but Nadeshot wasn’t giving up.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.360
Invited to participate at the MLG X Games Invitational,

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:08.980
the team had an important chance to get on the board against some of their biggest rivals.

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:15.280
"Going into that tournament I thought we could either place top 3 or we were going to get dead last.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:17.460
It was an invitational tournament, there were eight teams.

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:21.980
Practicing and scrims for us prior to the event were very up in the air

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:25.480
in terms of results. It was just really inconsistent."

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:31.180
The former compLexity roster that included ACHES signed with Evil Geniuses right before the event.

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:37.140
"Truthfully, I am a pretty realistic person, a little bit of a pessimist, so I was thinking the worst was coming."

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:40.460
And then, all of a sudden, we came out of the gate swinging.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:14:31.380
(Casting)

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:36.440
After defeating EG, OpTic defeated Team Kaliber in the finals to earn a gold medal.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:15:02.180
(Casting)

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:05.240
There was no prize pool and it was an invitational tournament,

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:09.240
but OpTic had found a victory in the middle of a difficult competitive season.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:13.380
"I don't know, I feel like I'm about to tear up. It's my first MLG event that I ever won,

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:15.420
I'm so happy that I won it with these guys.

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:20.220
Ever since I watched Halo 2 as a young kid on MLG, I dreamed about winning an MLG event.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:23.860
And for this to finally happen, plus a gold medal at the X Games

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.980
It's literally a dream come true."

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.660
Sadly, this would be the high point for the team’s year.

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:33.900
And as the team continued to struggle, Nadeshot increasingly became the subject of controversy.

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:36.840
As the team went to a Red Bull sponsored training camp,

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:40.980
Nadeshot and Scump were already looking for a replacement for ProofY.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:46.980
The answer would be Crimsix, and he wanted to add FormaL to the team so Clayster, too, was released.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:53.460
On paper, this roster was poised to take the 2015 CoD Advanced Warfare season by storm.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:56.020
The fresh game was a boon for Nadeshot.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:16:01.680
The team got off to a strong start. They earned first at UMG Orlando and the regular season of the

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:05.200
MLG Pro League Season 1. They won the playoffs, too,

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:09.200
and went on to dominate the CoD Championship NA Regional Finals.

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:13.540
But while the team was doing well, Nade felt like his play was deteriorating.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.720
His reactions weren’t enough to carry him through matches.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:20.500
And, when OpTic finished seventh at CoD Champs after their hot start,

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.080
Nadeshot knew that it would be his last event.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:29.720
I felt like my passion to win wasn’t high enough to continue at this level.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:33.320
To give you guys a mindset on what's been going through my head.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:39.240
I just felt like I was playing to not lose, I wasn’t really playing to win.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.440
So that I wouldn't have to hear about losing, the

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:46.040
repercussions of it on Twitter and on my YouTube channel and the week after.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:50.780
I was just so immensely afraid of the fact
that nobody would want to watch

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:54.980
my streams or my videos because I didn't have that role in OpTic Gaming anymore

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.600
and that is something that definitely kind

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.480
of hindered me from making that decision a little sooner.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:05.760
Three years of streaming, YouTube content and competition had pushed him to his limit,

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:09.900
but the comments blaming him for the team’s woes became overwhelming.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:14.420
I am a pretty self conscious person and with all these people being so hyper critical

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:19.060
about the way that I play and my role in that team… It got to me man,

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:23.620
and I’ve got pretty thick skin. But I just didn’t want to be the scapegoat anymore.

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:28.800
In hindsight, it’s surprising that he managed to juggle all these responsibilities for as long as he did.

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:31.880
And given the demands of esports competition today,

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:35.740
it’s unlikely that we’ll ever see it happen at his level again.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.580
What you might see is players saying

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:42.140
"I don't want to figure out that balance, I either want to be full-blown competition and dabble a bit,

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.920
or I want to be full blown content."

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:48.200
You can't just dabble in competition, right? You have to really, really focus.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:53.380
think that fork in the road is going to cause decisions but, for those who can maintain both,

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.780
more power to them. But it’s tough, it’s tough to do.

00:17:56.780 --> 00:18:01.400
Nadeshot has since created his own organization, 100 Thieves

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:04.100
In 2017 it was revealed that 100 Thieves

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:09.840
had secured a spot in the newly franchised NA LCS and had backing from Dan Gilbert,

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:11.840
the owner of the Cleveland Cavaliers.

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:16.300
In their first NA LCS split, 100 Thieves placed first in the regular season,

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:19.180
and Nadeshot was with the team every step of the way.

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:23.340
I'm so happy to be a part of these guys' careers and our team is awesome. And I

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:25.740
want to scream it from the mountain tops.

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:29.360
Call of Duty gave him his first big break, but it didn’t define him.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:33.180
And even now, as he cheers on the team that he both manages and owns,

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:37.700
it’s obvious that one of esports’ biggest stars is still that kid from Chicago.

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:40.140
So that's it YouTube, I'll see you f***ing later.

